<!--
    The status bar icon. Android draws it at 24dp, flattened to a single
    colour, often on a busy background next to a dozen others.

    It used to be a rod drawn as thin diagonal strokes, which at that size is
    not a rod, it is a stray slash. A solid carp silhouette survives the size,
    survives the flattening, and is recognisably this app at a glance - which
    is the whole job of the thing.

    evenOdd so the eye is a hole rather than a dot that vanishes when the icon
    is tinted.
-->
